# AGENTS.md

Machine-readable context for AI coding assistants (Cursor, Copilot, etc.).  
Copy to your **application repository root** and customize paths/tags.

## Commands

- Install: `npm install`
- Dev server: `npx nx serve <app-name>`
- Lint: `npx nx run-many -t lint`
- Test: `npx nx run-many -t test`
- E2E: `npx nx e2e <e2e-project>`
- Build: `npx nx build <app-name>`

## Repository layout

```text
apps/<demo-app>/          # Runnable application
apps/<demo>-e2e/          # Playwright E2E
libs/ports/               # Framework-free port interfaces ONLY
libs/adapters-mock/       # Demo/mock implementations
libs/adapters-<prod>/     # Production implementations (optional)
libs/shell/               # App shell, layout, global guards
libs/features-*/          # Domain features (auth, org, billing, …)
libs/ui/                  # Design system / Spartan helm components
```

## Architecture rules (ports & adapters)

1. **NEVER** import adapter libraries from `libs/features-*` or `libs/ui`.
2. Features inject ports via `InjectionToken` (e.g. `ORG_PORT`, `AUTH_PORT`, `BILLING_PORT`).
3. Swap mock vs production adapters only in `app.config.ts` (or `provide*Adapters()`).
4. `libs/ports` must not import `@angular/*` or `rxjs`.

## Nx tags (customize to match eslint depConstraints)

| Tag | May import |
|-----|------------|
| `type:port` | `type:util` only |
| `type:adapter` | `type:port` |
| `type:feature` | `type:port`, `type:ui`, `type:shell` |
| `type:ui` | `type:util` |

## Angular conventions

- Standalone components only (no new NgModules).
- Use `input()`, `output()`, `computed()` — avoid new `@Input` / `@Output`.
- Use `@if`, `@for`, `@switch` — avoid new `*ngIf` / `*ngFor`.
- Prefer `resource()` loaders calling port methods — avoid `subscribe()` in templates.
- Functional guards (`canActivateFn`) with `inject()`.

## Quality

- Rubric: [Quality Framework v1.0](https://github.com/oequ/quality-framework)
- Self-assessment: `docs/QUALITY.md` in this repo

## Do not

- Put Supabase/Firebase/Stripe SDKs in feature components.
- Use `bypassSecurityTrustHtml` without security review.
- Treat route guards as authorization (backend enforces access).
